23:T5bb,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the QR code generator free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. It is free to use, needs no sign-up and has no watermark on the downloaded image."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are my links or text stored by ContentVerse India?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The QR code is generated in your browser and the content you type is not sent to our servers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a QR code expire?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A static QR code does not expire. It only stops working if the page or link it points to goes offline."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need to pay to receive money through a QR code?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. You only need to enter your UPI PIN when you send money, never when you receive it. Be cautious of anyone asking you to scan a code to receive funds."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the QR Generator free on ContentVerse India?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. All India utility tools on ContentVerse India are free to use with no sign-up required."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this an official government website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. ContentVerse India is an independent platform. We use public datasets and open APIs. For official records, use government portals like Parivahan, GST, FoSCoS, or ECI."}}]}24:T7f5,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to use QR Generator","description":"A QR code turns a link, text or payment address into a square pattern that a phone camera can read in a second. This free QR code generator creates a QR for any URL, plain text or UPI payment link and lets you download it as a PNG image. It runs in your browser, so what you type is not uploaded to a","url":"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/qr-generator","totalTime":"PT5M","tool":{"@type":"HowToTool","name":"QR Generator"},"step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"How to create a QR code","text":"Type or paste the content into the box: a website address starting with https://, a line of text, or a UPI link such as upi://pay?pa=name@bank. The QR code updates as you type. When it looks right, press “Download PNG” and save the image."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"What you can put in a QR code","text":"The most common use is a website link: a restaurant menu, a Google review page, a form or a portfolio. QR codes can also carry plain text such as a Wi-Fi password note, a phone number or an address. For payments in India, a UPI link that includes the payee’s VPA and, optionally, the name and amount lets customers pay from any UPI app."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Printing and design tips","text":"Print the code at least 2 cm by 2 cm for close scanning and larger for posters. Keep a quiet margin of white space around it, use dark modules on a light background and avoid placing it on a curved or reflective surface. Low contrast, such as light grey on white, is the most common reason a code fails."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Safety: scanning and sharing QR codes","text":"Scammers sometimes paste fake QR codes over genuine ones or send codes that ask you to “scan to receive money”. You never need to scan a code or enter a UPI PIN to receive money. Check the payee name shown in your UPI app before you pay, and avoid scanning codes from unknown messages."}]}19:[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"QR Generator\",\"alternateName\":\"QR Code Generator — Free Online\",\"description\":\"Generate a QR code from any text, URL, UPI ID, or Wi‑Fi string. Download as PNG instantly — free, no sign-up.\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/qr-generator\",\"applicationCategory\":\"UtilitiesApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Any\",\"browserRequirements\":\"Requires JavaScript\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"0\",\"priceCurrency\":\"INR\"},\"provider\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"ContentVerse India\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-IN\",\"featureList\":\"How to create a QR code, What you can put in a QR code, Printing and design tips, Safety: scanning and sharing QR codes\"}"}}],["$","script","1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$23"}}],["$","script","2",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"India Tools\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"QR Generator\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/qr-generator\"}]}"}}],["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$24"}}]],"$L25"]
